{
  "requirement": "The `PlainText` implementation of `OutlineLang` supplies the extension, selection, and fingerprint rules described in this chapter.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct PlainText;\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for PlainText;\nimpl Debug for PlainText;\nimpl Default for PlainText;\nimpl OutlineLang for PlainText;\nimpl Copy for PlainText;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.PlainText` declares the `PlainText` unit struct and its trait implementations: Clone, Debug, Default, Copy and `OutlineLang`. It says the type supplies the extension, selection and fingerprint rules described in the chapter. Those rules are the obligations of the refining requirements `plain-text.items` and `plain-text.fingerprints`. They need no separate test under this requirement.\n\nCoverage of what this requirement states:\n- **Type exists and is public.** `tests/outline_content.rs#fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` constructs `languages::PlainText` as a unit value. `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the export inventory against rustdoc and checks that the Habeas consumer compiles.\n- **`OutlineLang` implementation, extension rule.** The same bundled-languages test asserts `plain.name() == \"plain-text\"` and `plain.extensions().is_empty()`. That is the claim of no extensions.\n- **`OutlineLang` implementation, selection and outline.** `unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors` goes through `OutlineContent::from_source`, which falls back to `PlainText`. It asserts these things:\n  - The root item has span 0..18.\n  - Each non-blank line becomes a `line` item.\n  - Selectors have the form `line@<12 hex digits>` and match the structural hash prefix.\n  - Duplicate lines share a selector, while different lines do not.\n  - `select` returns the line text.\n  - The empty source gives a single root item.\n- **`OutlineLang` implementation, fingerprints.** `plain_line_fingerprints_use_sha256_words_without_losing_boundaries` asserts a known SHA-256 value, whitespace normalisation, word-boundary preservation, and the scheme string `plain-text-structural-v1:own-v1`.\n- **`OutlineLang` implementation, structural search.** `outline_only_languages_report_unsupported_structural_search` asserts that `PlainText.search_structure` returns an error mentioning plain-text. This test carries no `{test}` marker for this requirement. It is extra evidence and is not needed for the verdict.\n\nThe Clone, Copy, Debug and Default implementations come from `#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]` in the `language!` macro in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/languages/mod.rs`. They have no conditionals and no transformations, so they fall under the exemption for untested obligations that need no code of their own. The compile-time public-API check also covers them.\n\nI found no unacknowledged gaps and no `{fixme}` acknowledgments.",
